Hi Elizabeth,

One item to add to Jeffrey's note. It concerns the plan document, not the cen=
sus, but we need both before we calculate any benefit.

A valuation measures the benefits the plan actually promises as of the valuat=
ion date. That means the provisions as amended, not as originally written. A =
provision we have to infer becomes an assumption, and we avoid making one whe=
re a document exists.

Please send the current plan document for Howard and Sons, with each amendmen=
t adopted since it was last restated. If there have been no amendments, a one=
-line reply saying so is enough. The secure file site is the best route for t=
he document itself.

Once it is in hand, David will code the provisions into the model alongside t=
he census. We will then send you a short summary of the data and provisions a=
s we have them, kept separate from any assumption.

Sincerely,
Jennifer


